```
# ============================================================================
# Detection: Windows Event Log Cleared
# Detection ID: DE-DE-001
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1070.001 - Indicator Removal: Clear Windows Event Logs
# Data Source: Windows Security 1102 / System 104
# Severity: Critical
# ============================================================================

index=endpoint sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=1102
| eval first_seen=strftime(_time,"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| table first_seen, ComputerName, SubjectUserName, SubjectDomainName
| append
    [ search index=endpoint sourcetype="WinEventLog:System" EventCode=104
      | eval first_seen=strftime(_time,"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
      | table first_seen, ComputerName, User_Name as SubjectUserName ]
| sort -first_seen
```

## Detection Logic
Event 1102 (Security log cleared) and 104 (any log cleared, System channel) are almost never legitimate outside of scoped log-rotation maintenance. This is one of the highest-fidelity indicators of an active intruder covering tracks post-compromise.

## False Positive Considerations
Log rotation scripts run by sanctioned automation accounts on a schedule — allowlist that single service account and alert on any other principal.

## Tuning Notes
This should be a Tier-1 immediate page, not a triage-queue alert, given near-zero false positive rate outside change-managed maintenance.
